Master CCNA Lab

This is my comprehensive CCNA practical lab, combining the networking concepts and technologies covered throughout my CCNA studies into a single integrated network environment.

## Lab Environment

### Physical Cisco Equipment

- Cisco 1841 Routers
- Cisco Catalyst 3550 Series Switches

### Virtual Lab Platforms

- GNS3
- Cisco Packet Tracer

## Technologies Implemented

### Switching

- VLANs
- Access Ports
- Trunking
- Inter-VLAN Routing
- VTP
- STP
- EtherChannel

### Routing

- Static Routing
- Default Routing
- OSPF
- Routing Table Analysis

### Network Services

- DHCP
- NAT
- PAT
- DNS Fundamentals

### Network Security

- Standard ACL
- Extended ACL
- Port Security
- SSH
- Secure Device Access

### Troubleshooting

- Layer 1 Troubleshooting
- Layer 2 Troubleshooting
- Layer 3 Troubleshooting
- Routing Troubleshooting
- Connectivity Testing

## Verification

Common verification commands used throughout the lab include:

```text
show ip interface brief
show vlan brief
show interfaces trunk
show spanning-tree
show etherchannel summary
show ip route
show ip protocols
show ip ospf neighbor
show ip dhcp binding
show ip nat translations
show access-lists
ping
traceroute
